Subject: [PATCH 6/8] security(V-23a): account-deletion scope manifest + CI
 completeness test
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

accountDeletion.ts declared the uid-keyed root collections as a static inline
allowlist (['voip_outbound','fcm_outbound']); a future uid-keyed root collection
added elsewhere would silently escape GDPR Art.17 erasure. Move the inventory to
accountDeletionRootCollections.ts as a single-source-of-truth manifest (delete/exempt
+ reason + handledBy), derive ROOT_COLLECTIONS_KEYED_BY_UID from it (behavior
identical), and add a completeness test that scans functions/src for
.collection("X").where("uid", ...) and FAILS CI if any discovered root
uid-keyed collection is unclassified (mirrors the BOLA catalog-completeness pattern).
Scan currently finds voip_outbound, fcm_outbound, provider_account_secret_refs — all
classified. tsc clean; 4 vitest cases green. [opus-implemented+verified]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
